  "verificationNotes": "Owner-authorized publication-first testing used one authenticated Cloudflare API MCP OAuth session to capture the provider tools/list catalog (4 code-mode tools, one page, server cloudflare-api 0.1.0, protocol 2025-06-18). All four tools are pinned with exact observed input schemas; search and execute carry reviewed condensed descriptions because the provider descriptions exceed the 1000-character catalog bound. execute runs arbitrary Cloudflare API requests, carries the provider destructiveHint, and requires approval; docs, search, and whoami are read tools. The 62 requested scopes are the required bootstrap scopes, developer-platform and account or zone reads, and bounded developer-platform writes (Workers scripts and routes, KV, R2, D1, Queues, Pages, DNS, cache purge, Secrets Store, observability, Workers CI, Workers AI, Vectorize, Containers, Browser Rendering, Pipelines, R2 Data Catalog); zone.write and account administration writes are excluded. The capture requested a 219-scope superset of this set and was granted exactly the requested scopes, a 3600-second bearer token, a refresh token, and the iss authorization-response parameter. The consent page lets the Owner narrow scopes; any narrowed grant fails the exact-match scope policy closed. Identity is the whoami structured id, documented as stable. Token-only revocation at the token endpoint returned 401; revocation is declared with the registration client identity. Live consent through the application, privacy review, and production acceptance remain pending."
}
